ver, the same source also notes that A can be unorganized and sometimes does not take criticism well, suggesting possible inconsistencies in day\u2011to\u2011day reliability.\n**Stress resilience** \u2013\u202fI have no specific information in my notes about how Candidate\u202fA performs under pressure or in crisis situations.\n**Crew cooperation** \u2013\u202fThe \u201cvery good leadership qualities\u201d attributed to A imply an ability to work constructively with a crew and to contribute positively to the cockpit environment. The comment that A is sometimes not good at taking criticism could, however, hinder collaborative dynamics if feedback is needed.\n**Professional communication** \u2013\u202fThe only communication\u2011related observation for A is that they are sometimes not good at taking criticism, which points to a potential weakness in receiving and responding to feedback. No other explicit evidence about respectful or effective communication with colleagues is available."}
